  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: All 6 completed experiments used multiprofile with aggregation (transformer or avgpool). The best result (config_010, acc=0.7250) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. scvi_n200 is clearly the best RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l the best image encoder, transformer the best aggregation, and weighted the best fusion. However, the profile_setting dimension (singleprofile vs multiprofile) is completely untested. Question: config_003 tests whether a singleprofile architecture (no aggregation step) with the best-known encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) and best fusion (weighted) can match or exceed the multiprofile pipeline. This is the largest unexplored design axis. Rationale: With only 3 experiments remaining after this one, resolving whether the multiprofile+aggregation pipeline is actually necessary (vs. a simpler singleprofile approach) is the highest-information experiment. If singleprofile is competitive, it opens a new search direction; if not, it confirms we should exploit the multiprofile+transformer+weighted cluster in the final experiments. All other untested configs are small perturbations of already-explored settings unlikely to beat 0.7250."
}

